dialect protocol
protocol stdio.zip.diff
version 1
schema stdio.zip
start diff
framing record

# P2-P2: REAL binary diff frame, replacing F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (per the P2-W0 census, 100% of stdio's `DiffCodec::encode` impls were still on it — see
# ../🦀️component.rs's upgraded `impl protocol::DiffCodec for ZipDiff`, `#region 🔖️BinaryDiffCodec`).
# `ZipDiff` is FLAT — unlike json's self-recursive `JsonValue`, neither `comment` nor `entries` is
# a recursive value type, so the top-level shape genuinely IS two independent optional sections,
# and the header below is real, walkable, non-opaque:
#
# `format` (=1) + `has_comment` (0/1) + `has_entries` (0/1) as three real fixed `u8` fields.
#
# What stays opaque is only the VARIABLE part: when present, `comment` is a length-prefixed UTF-8
# string, and `entries` is three runtime-counted lists (`removed`: names; `modified`: name +
# sparse per-field patch; `added`: index + a whole 14-field `ZipEntry`) — this dialect's `Array`
# primitive repeats one FIXED-WIDTH `Prim`, not a repeated multi-field RECORD of varying per-item
# shape, so a count-prefixed list of `ZipEntryDiff`/`ZipEntry` records has no field-by-field walk
# at this declarative layer today (the same category of gap as json's `Prim::Ref` recursion —
# filed in this wave's `mechanism_gaps`). The Rust `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side IS genuinely
# real, structured, recursively-typed binary (`enc_entry_bin`/`enc_entries_diff_bin` in the same
# file, LEB128-varint-framed via `store::pack_rt::write_varint_u64`/`store::ByteReader`) — this
# protocol file honestly bounds only what it can field-by-field walk.

field format u8
field has_comment u8
field has_entries u8
chain payload bytes
